// flow_rate is how much of a cell's fill (0..1000) may transfer to a
// neighbour per tick, in the compressible-volume liquid model -- see
// update.rs's module doc. Higher looks runnier and settles flat faster;
// lower looks viscous. (dispersion is Gas kind's equivalent, not this
// material's -- Liquid kind ignores it.)
//
// 1000 (i.e. no cap below a cell's own full fill) is deliberate, not an
// oversight: `transfer_liquid_horizontal` already bounds each tick's
// actual transfer to half the src/dst difference (see that function's own
// doc for why -- transferring more overshoots and oscillates forever), so
// flow_rate only ever throttles *on top of* that halving. At the original
// 200, flow_rate was the binding constraint for any pool more than a
// handful of cells wide, and a wide pool poured onto an unwalled ledge
// stayed visibly sloped -- sand-pile-shaped, not flat -- for hundreds to
// thousands of frames while flow_rate-limited transfers cascaded outward
// one small hop at a time (reported directly from a live playtest
// screenshot; reproduced with a debug harness pouring water on two
// separate floating ledges and confirmed the same trapezoidal shape).
// Removing flow_rate as a *second*, redundant bottleneck lets the halving
// rule alone govern convergence speed, which converges geometrically
// (each step closes half the remaining gap) rather than linearly.
(
    name: "water",
    display: "Water",
    kind: Liquid,
    density: 1.0,
    flow_rate: 1000,
    // Dead band: below this fill difference two adjacent cells stop trading.
    // 16 is flat but slow; 60 roughly halves settling time (and so how long
    // a pool keeps its chunks awake) for a ~0.5% surface slope that is not
    // visible. Live-tunable with `O` -- sweep it on real water rather than
    // guessing. See `MaterialDef::min_transfer` for the measurements.
    min_transfer: 16,
    // How much a partially-filled cell dims toward black, 0..1. 0.65 is the
    // long-standing look. Lower it if the settled waterline reads as a
    // mottled band rather than a clean edge: only ~1% of a resting body's
    // cells are partial, but they are all at the surface, and their fill
    // ranges widely enough to draw anywhere from ~54% to 100% brightness.
    // Live-tunable with `O`.
    fill_dimming: 0.0,
    colors: [
        (64, 116, 208),
        (58, 108, 198),
        (72, 126, 218),
    ],
)
